# Dogfood pack: a request-supplied name must not reach a filesystem handle.
#
# `LogFileReader.Resolve(service, file)` normalises the name and then prefixes it with
# the log root before constructing a `FileInfo`. `Path.GetFullPath` is declared a
# sanitiser here because the code's real guard is the pair `IsSegment(file)` and the
# `PathEquals(GetDirectoryName(full), dir)` prefix check — the EDB has no guard facts,
# so the pack states the effect the guard has as a sanitiser assumption. The proof is
# only as strong as that assumption; see the note's friction list.
rule log-path
  kind taint
  severity error
  message A request-supplied name reaches a filesystem handle
  source Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.HttpRequest.get_Headers result
  source Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.HttpRequest.get_Query result
  sanitise System.IO.Path.GetFullPath result
  sanitise System.IO.Path.GetFileName result
  sink System.IO.FileInfo..ctor arg 0
  sink System.IO.FileStream..ctor arg 0
end
